        "title": "refactor(agents): trim embedded runner exports",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe production-mode Knip baseline still carried 22 unused exports around the embedded agent runner facade, attempt helpers, run state, and context guard.\n\nRelated: #105595\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Remove redundant embedded-runner and attempt re-exports.\n- Point tests at the canonical owning modules instead of keeping facade aliases alive for tests.\n- Delete the now-test-only stream-resolution cache reset; the test already uses a fresh session object.\n- Make the preemptive overflow message private and keep the exact behavior assertion local to the test.\n- Regenerate the baseline against current main, including three unrelated pairing entries newly exposed by main drift. Net baseline change remains shrink-only: 19 fewer entries globally and 22 fewer under src/agents.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNone. Internal export-surface cleanup only; embedded run behavior is unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm deadcode:exports:update`: stable pre/post baseline hash, 5,622 entries.\n- `pnpm deadcode:exports`: passed.\n- src/agents baseline: 516 -> 494 entries.\n- Focused remote Vitest proof: 274 tests passed across unit-fast, agents, and e2e shards.\n- `pnpm check:changed`: conflict markers, changelog attribution, export guards, duplicate coverage, dependency pins, formatting, Plugin SDK API baseline, package patch guard, core typecheck, core-test typecheck, and the touched src/agents lint shard passed. Testbox killed the process with exit 137 later in the unrelated src/daemon lint shard.\n- Fresh autoreview: clean; no accepted/actionable findings.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n\nNo changelog: internal dead-export cleanup only.\n",
